ASC BRASS CAP 10CM BGL, LANDSCAPED.3.7M NE OF Face of curb; 4.5M SE OF TRANSFORMER #310 STA 26U</groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="684623908">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP270 St. Albert 

Out grabbing a few more BCPs on the last day for logging them. Parked on the opposite side of Grandin from the cap so made the quick walk over. I didn't initially notice but I caught the attention of a father walking home with his kids. I made the find quickly, cleared off a bit of leaf debris and then took some pics. As I was turning to leave I noticed the father wondering what I was up to. Once I crossed back to the car I saw he moved on. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks outforthehunt for all the BCPs and the fun I've had over the last couple weeks getting most of the ones in the Edmonton area. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684115509">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-05T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP270 St. Albert&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I parked on Tache at the public parking next to the CITO cap and walked over to grab this one first.  It was a nice walk today on the first hot, hot day we've had this year.  Once close to GZ area it took me just a few minutes to spot the hole.  :)  A bit of traffic going by but that was no problem.  I snapped my pics and then headed back to find the other cap close to the car.  TFTBC OFTH!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
